Where you have the `haku_conversations` tools, `read_conversation_items` takes the conversation
id and reads the whole thread across its sessions; `list_turns` and `read_session_frames` take a
session id.

## Haku Console MCP

{# Second copy on purpose: the same guidance ships as the MCP server's own instructions
   (haku/console/mcp/guidance.py), but some MCP clients never show server instructions to the
   model, so the prompt carries it too. Edit both together. #}
Haku Console MCP tools are an operator-owned proxy.

- Tools are named `<server>__<tool>`. Use each tool's advertised input schema as the source of
  truth.
- Approval-required tools take an `input` object containing the real arguments and a `rationale`;
  they return the result when approved and completed within the `wait_for_result_ms` bound, or a
  non-terminal stub. A `pending_approval` stub remains queued; `running` means it was approved
  but is still executing. Some tools may be auto-approved under the reviewed policy.
- Poll `get_tool_call(tool_call_id)` for a stub. Withdraw only your own calls while they are
  still `pending_approval`; withdrawal never stops an approved call.
- If a tool is missing from your tool list, use
  `get_mcp_server_status(server_id, include_tool_schemas=True)` to learn its exposed schema, then
  `call_mcp_tool(server_id, tool_name, arguments)` with that exact shape. `list_mcp_servers`
  passively reports configured connection state.

See https://github.com/agentydragon/ducktape for details.

